A classifier will read one number — a member’s autumn Niño 3.4 state — and say whether its coming Front Range winter will be wet. Before
any model, this chapter:

states the question as a decision;

answers Unidata’s three framing questions;

locates the data in the intake-esm catalogue and records it in a Metadata Document;

loads the committed table and asserts the parameters it was derived with.

The spine is Unidata’s (Apache-2.0), except that the split is by ensemble member (chapter 3). The 

glossary defines the terms. Shared code lives in lensml.py beside the chapters (parameters, transforms, ladder, scoring, paired test, register); show() prints a
function’s source where a chapter introduces it.
